#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31bd6c00-f798-5f52-8846-d0354e446d46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302590} {:answer/id #uuid "0f790dec-57a6-50e2-ae78-aecfd1e526bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302591} {:answer/id #uuid "3018ea92-63a7-573e-b157-ec5f717b1254" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302592} {:answer/id #uuid "1de88b45-c080-5a50-be90-5f0c5be697c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302593} {:answer/id #uuid "3569ca0f-f09b-58e7-b673-c4e366db8821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f790dec-57a6-50e2-ae78-aecfd1e526bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302591} :answer-field/id #uuid "12fc5801-5621-5551-975d-5ccdd051d75a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6b7394b-01c9-52bb-809f-2cab825b18da" :question/math-academy-id "q-115129" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041013/assets/c71a52cc148f8ce4a23a2fb2005757c9d141d3caf05586d8fb5122f591dc7474.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=1$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51a28714-a125-53b7-8a56-9d8e5eb5fd8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310306} {:answer/id #uuid "33472bbc-2958-5b76-9fd7-e4be00b37d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33472bbc-2958-5b76-9fd7-e4be00b37d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310307} :answer-field/id #uuid "de0b8d34-f76b-543f-ad36-2d004571145a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310305} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc2e44ce-3a5b-51df-aea3-bff0213280ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc2e44ce-3a5b-51df-aea3-bff0213280ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310309} :answer-field/id #uuid "8274bf2f-e625-59e7-8f11-4a513638b6af" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f865070-f5b3-5500-a742-b83f4ec5d86b" :question/math-academy-id "q-279165" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=9$ and ${b}^{2}=4.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=9,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=4,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=3,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 3=6,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aaeb91a-64e6-5fec-8909-27232704b53b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4aaeb91a-64e6-5fec-8909-27232704b53b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310312} :answer-field/id #uuid "93b4a93e-f7aa-53d4-8e4f-f1ff1353c830" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310311} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cc8fa3e-a39d-560c-adf0-fe9d14532ffa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cc8fa3e-a39d-560c-adf0-fe9d14532ffa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310314} :answer-field/id #uuid "61154251-8d8a-58c7-b516-d8b455260b49" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310313}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7f34816-fae1-5bab-b494-08ab8f5462c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-279166" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=36$ and ${b}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=36,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 4=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4102dd04-292b-5aa0-be43-eaca3f7b98e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302622} {:answer/id #uuid "341d6331-272c-53ad-8d6c-f724841c85a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302623} {:answer/id #uuid "d9221f3e-391d-51e6-8eeb-3c9323e17425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302624} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b7fde4-ca32-5996-a1e5-665eb886edf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302625} {:answer/id #uuid "062d034f-943a-5896-a335-90c666e01815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{10}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0b7fde4-ca32-5996-a1e5-665eb886edf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302625} :answer-field/id #uuid "30ca1e55-10d3-51da-aece-ec767a7ef1d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60ed3df5-f374-5da1-8a03-7183d44bf408" :question/math-academy-id "q-69893" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041013/assets/be8468d84e3820bd1e9181d31aa3a1b7d1a85c743020a69cb67fc3f601a88363.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93208ab8-b7f9-502f-9388-6b27e7ddaaf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086522} {:answer/id #uuid "bad95e2b-9741-57e9-9007-4f7486526529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086523} {:answer/id #uuid "e80e0064-3613-5c06-8aa0-c564fb94a355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086524} {:answer/id #uuid "343b5696-c3b0-54bf-8c62-39eed419a557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086525} {:answer/id #uuid "7c224b89-dfa5-5ea2-9617-375e674cb6a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bad95e2b-9741-57e9-9007-4f7486526529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086523} :answer-field/id #uuid "a531362f-6025-5d1f-b380-fb75d357e191" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b586f348-117c-513c-b7f9-86528f54bc6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-7598" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=4,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 4=8,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4.$"}]}
